text:
Due to the COVID pandemic, this review will present it's constructive criticism in a light-hearted tone. 

The app (for mobile/Android) was efficient, comprehensive, and easy to use. Order was ready on time, and it was promptly delivered to my car when I arrived at the 5:30 p.m. designated time and after I checked in on the app. The young woman who brought it out was smiling and genuinely seemed pleased to assist us. "Have a great rest of your evening!" she said as we got ready to pull out. Got home in approx 5 mins. 

Opened containers of cold food (per receipt left the kitchen at 4:59) to find a kitchen staff in Bellevue (37221) who don't give a damn.

- You can't classify 5 pieces of lettuce shoved in a little cup as a "ceasar salad."
- Bone-in wings were dry as *@#$ and the extra buffalo sauce that was paid for never showed for the party;
- Same for extra ranch and salsa for our half-filled bag of chips; 
- Cheese was nonexistent...in a QUESAdilla;
- Yes it was a pile of flaky, yet hard, tortillas scarcely packed with a substance pretending to be "chicken, bacon, ranch," but mostly just dry, crispy tortillas.

Ordered utensils were not provided, but the pomegranate juice, I-I-I mean... margaritas, were delicious. For real tho, if those had alcohol in them, it snuck past our detectors.

In all, no, I likely won't be back soon for mediocre imposters of good-sounding food and drink from a place that cannot prepare the most basic of recipes. Sorry.
